<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1088" root="الك" body-key="A">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَكَ الِلّجَامَ</span></b> , (ISd, K,) [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَلُكَ</span></b>  or 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَلِكَ</span></b> ,] inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلْكٌ</span>, (ISd, TA,) <i>He</i> (a horse) <i>chewed,</i> or <i>champed,
the bit;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَكَهُ</span>. (ISd, K.) One says, of a
horse, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يألكُ اللُّجُمَ</span> <i>He chews,</i> or <i>champs, the bits:</i>
but the verb commonly known is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَلُوكَ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَعْلُكُ</span>.
(Lth.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence, accord. to some, (see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلُوكٌ</span>,)]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَكَ بَيْنَ القَوْمِ</span>, (Msb, TA,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَلِكَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلْكٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُلُوكٌ</span>, (Msb,) <i>He acted as a messenger</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَسَّلَ</span>)
<i>between the people.</i> (Msb, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَكَهُ</span>,
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَلِكَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلْكٌ</span>, <i>He conveyed,</i> or <i>communicated,
to him a message.</i> (Kr.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَكَ</span> <i>He sent.</i>
(IB in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوك</span>.)

